course: dictionary
lesson: 9511
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One small word can have several meanings, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. Stick is a good example, because it can name a thing or describe an action. Try each meaning in the sentence to see which one fits.
explain: «Super glue sticks skin together in seconds» uses stick as a verb: to fix one thing to another. Here sticks means joins with glue. Only an adult should use super glue.
explain: «A fish hook stuck in a finger is not pulled out» uses stuck as a verb, meaning pushed into something and held there. An adult or doctor removes it, because the barb tears skin.
explain: The word changes its form: stick, sticks, stuck, sticking. «Then, thump! thump! she lands on a heap of sticks and dry leaves» uses sticks as a noun, meaning thin pieces of wood, often fallen from a tree.
fact: Stick can be a noun (a thing) or a verb (an action), so check the sentence to see which one it is.
fact: A stick is a thin piece of wood, often fallen from a tree, or a long thin thing such as a hockey stick or a stick of celery.
fact: To stick is to fix one thing to another with glue or tape, or to push a pointed thing into something, as in «stick a pin in».
fact: To stick can mean to become fixed and unable to move, as in «the door sticks».
fact: To stick with something means to keep doing it.
exercise: «Super glue sticks skin together in seconds.» What does sticks mean here? | Pushes a pointed thing into something | Keeps doing something without stopping | *Fixes one thing to another with glue | Walks with a long thin pole
exercise: «Then, thump! thump! she lands on a heap of sticks and dry leaves.» What are the sticks? | Long, sharp needles from a pine | Glue sticks for school | *Thin pieces of wood, often fallen from a tree | Dry, crunchy biscuits
exercise: Ben says, «The door sticks.» What does sticks mean? | Makes a loud bang | Is painted a bright colour | Opens very quickly | *Becomes fixed and unable to move
test: «A fish hook stuck in a finger is not pulled out.» What does stuck mean here? | Washed clean under a tap | Glued neatly to a page | Hidden under a dry leaf | *Pushed into something and held there
test: In «Use a glue stick to fix the card», what kind of word is stick? | A verb, an action | *A noun, a thing | An adverb, a word about how | An adjective, a describing word
exam: Which sentence uses stick as a noun? | *«Then, thump! thump! she lands on a heap of sticks and dry leaves.» | «Wet skin on very cold metal freezes and sticks to it.» | «Clothes stick together after the tumble dryer.» | «Super glue sticks skin together in seconds.»
